251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Symposia\) are one-day, student-led events where the content and logistics are owned by Cloud Club Captains. Student Community Days can be in person, hybrid, or fully online. Its content should suit your members, focusing on AWS skills and career advice. Student Community Days are a way to bring AWS learning onto campus. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The event audience is primarily Cloud Club members, but can be extended to non-member students, space permitting. Students are responsible for the content of the event. If needed, Captains may request AWS speaker\(s\) for their event. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
253 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The first Student Symposium was held at the Heinz College in Carnegie Mellon University, and was hosted by three Cloud Club Captains for a day of learning. It included two tracks: a series of guest lectures and a hands-on workshop.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
